WEBVTT

00:00:01.610 --> 00:00:05.230
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:10.240
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.530
This is the story of
their lives and adventures.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:22.260
It’s finally here!

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:23.440
What is?

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:26.190
The e-mail from Project Mew!

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:27.060
Really?!

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.910
Huh? What’s going on?

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:30.430
Haven’t you heard?

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:36.140
Some people put together a deep-dive search team
for Mew, and they’re recruiting new members.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:42.390
Go is facing their membership test
after Professor Okido recommended him.

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:44.590
Well? What does the e-mail say?

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:46.470
Are you heading out on a Trial Mission?

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:52.430
“Visit our laboratory
at the base of Mount Tengan in Sinnoh.”

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:55.320
Since when do they have a lab there?

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:56.820
Let’s not sweat it
till we’re there.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:57.850
Yeah!

00:00:57.850 --> 00:00:59.290
Wait, you’re coming with me?

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:00.740
You kidding me?

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:02.990
I said I’d cheer you on!

00:01:02.990 --> 00:01:04.240
Thanks!

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:05.250
Then, here goes...

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:07.880
Let’s go!

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:48.100
Following
Project Mew’s instructions,

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:53.020
Satoshi and Go have gone off to
the foot of Sinnoh’s Mount Tengan.

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:56.600
What lies in store for them?

00:02:57.430 --> 00:02:59.260
Is that really it?

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:02.910
The map says
this should be the right place...

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:05.910
But that doesn’t really
look like a lab.

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:09.650
Shigeru!

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:16.650
Oh? Who else would it be
but Satoshi, and...

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:17.940
Uh...

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:18.910
Go!

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:22.940
So you’re trying out, too.
I heard the news.

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:24.430
That’s why I’m here!

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:30.370
Well, seems even an inept trainer can try his luck
if he has a recommendation from a professor.

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:33.520
But only what you do
from here on counts.

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:35.460
What are you implying?

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:39.530
I’m saying Project Mew
is not exactly going to be easy.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.230
Well, try your best,
at the very least.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:49.860
He makes me <i>furious!</i>

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:53.040
That’s Shigeru for ya...

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:56.320
Hello!

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:59.610
Excuse me!

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:09.250
What’s wrong, Manene?

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:15.070
Hi! I had an e-mail
telling me to come here...

00:04:16.070 --> 00:04:17.690
Oh, good timing!

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:23.010
Th-This is heavy...

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:28.370
Is something wrong?

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:31.080
There’s a trick to opening this...

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:35.510
Easy... does it...

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:38.670
Hah... So heavy, so bulky.

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:41.050
This is why I hate paper documents...

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:46.340
Is that... Mew?!

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:47.840
Let me see!

00:04:48.730 --> 00:04:52.730
Everything in this room
is data on Mew.

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:55.550
Everything?

00:04:55.550 --> 00:04:57.840
Yes. But it’s not enough.

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:00.620
For every book here,
I’ve read dozens more,

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:02.240
but the mystery only deepens.

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:04.750
Searching for Mew...

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:07.300
It makes me feel like
I’m losing myself deep in a maze.

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:11.740
But at the same time,
it’s strangely nostalgic.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:15.490
I never did introduce myself.

00:05:16.490 --> 00:05:17.460
I’m Hodaka.

00:05:18.890 --> 00:05:21.210
The leader of Project Mew.

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:23.170
Leader?!

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:26.180
Go! Nice to meet you!

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:29.110
Professor Okido told me
about you.

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:30.110
You can handle the rest.

00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:30.930
Right.

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:35.050
The woman Shigeru was talking to!

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:37.060
The name’s Asahi.

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:39.470
As you are aware...

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:44.940
Project Mew is an enormous project
aiming to conduct an exhaustive search for Mew.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:49.570
We will conduct the search
atop Table Mountain, on this island.

00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:54.300
Composed of sedimentary rocks
dating back two billion years,

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:58.620
it’s the world’s largest mountain by surface area,
at roughly 40,000 square kilometers,

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:01.630
and it’s over 3,500 meters tall.

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:03.840
Awesome! I wanna go there!

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:06.470
Where is that island?

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:08.220
Is Mew there?

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:10.720
Save your questions for the end.

00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:13.600
She’s pretty strict...

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:15.210
Just wait for now.

00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:19.730
The project will take place during the one week
where it switches from wet season to dry season.

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:23.230
When the week is over,
the dampness returns to the area,

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:26.450
covering it in a thick fog
and making exploration impossible.

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:28.480
Any questions?

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:32.030
Um... About Mew...

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:34.830
Details about Mew are confidential.

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:37.120
If you have any other questions,
then go ahead.

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:39.620
No questions, then.

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:42.860
Next, about our recruitment.

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:48.130
Prospective members have to clear
the Trial Missions we assign.

00:06:48.550 --> 00:06:50.380
That’s what Shigeru was doing!

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:54.000
The missions test your knowledge
as a Pokémon Trainer,

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:58.720
your overall capturing skills,
orders and partnership in battles,

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:01.650
and your teamwork with other trainers,
among other things.

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:03.840
What was that?

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:05.390
Silence, please.

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:06.400
Right!

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:08.860
Upon clearing a Trial Mission,

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:12.280
a token will be sent
to the challenger’s Smartphone Rotom.

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:19.040
The candidates with the most tokens
when the testing period ends, will pass.

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:21.530
This time,
we’re looking for three people.

00:07:21.530 --> 00:07:23.560
Together with the two
already selected,

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:28.420
the official active Mew search team
will be made up of five Chasers.

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:30.060
Chasers...

00:07:30.060 --> 00:07:32.370
They’ve already chosen people for it...

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:35.140
Are you one of them, Ms. Asahi?

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:40.600
Yes. The two already selected are me
and one other, a man named Tsurugi.

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:42.140
Tsurugi...

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:43.460
Any other questions?

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:44.390
Yeah!

00:07:44.390 --> 00:07:46.230
Can I help?

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:50.970
Teamwork with your allies
is an important criterion evaluated in the missions.

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:51.930
It’s fine.

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:53.360
All right!

00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:55.370
It should nearly be time.

00:08:05.090 --> 00:08:07.130
We’re flying?!

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:10.870
This is the ice field
north of Mount Tengan.

00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:16.010
Go. We will have you catch
an Alolan Kyukon in this area.

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:21.390
Kyukon! Alolan Form!
Fox Pokémon! Ice/Fairy type!

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:23.270
Possesses a calm demeanor!

00:08:23.270 --> 00:08:27.410
It lives on a secluded snowy mountain
where a deity resides,

00:08:27.410 --> 00:08:32.180
so it was revered as the deity’s incarnation
before it was identified as a regional form of Kyukon!

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:34.160
A mountain where a deity resides?

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:37.230
Lanakila Mountain in Alola!

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:41.450
But that means
there won’t be any of them here...

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:45.790
I’ve given you your mission.

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:49.300
It’s up to you to decide
what you’ll do next.

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:52.000
I’ll catch it, no question!

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:53.550
That’s what I like to hear!

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:57.420
Your time limit is six hours.

00:08:57.420 --> 00:08:59.810
Make sure you’re back here by then.

00:08:59.810 --> 00:09:01.270
Right!

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:02.050
Let’s go.

00:09:02.050 --> 00:09:02.930
Yeah!

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:10.840
Everyone, help us out!

00:09:25.670 --> 00:09:28.790
Well, I wasn’t expecting it
to be easy to find...

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:31.040
Where’s it hiding?

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:34.070
Oh, they’re back!

00:09:36.250 --> 00:09:37.990
Hmm... No luck, then?

00:09:37.990 --> 00:09:39.450
Return for now.

00:09:39.450 --> 00:09:40.680
Thanks!

00:09:43.330 --> 00:09:45.890
That just leaves Hassam...

00:09:48.390 --> 00:09:49.840
That’s Hassam’s voice!

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:51.310
Let’s go!

00:09:51.310 --> 00:09:52.110
Yeah!

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:05.910
There it is!

00:10:06.310 --> 00:10:08.110
Good job, Hassam!

00:10:10.140 --> 00:10:11.740
It’s beautiful...

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:20.090
Go! Are you okay?!

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:22.010
Yeah!

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:23.100
But what’s going on...?!

00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:26.730
The Index said it had
a calm demeanor...

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:31.120
It’s really angry...

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:39.060
Satoshi!
What’s good against an Ice/Fairy type?!

00:10:39.060 --> 00:10:40.230
Steel type!

00:10:40.230 --> 00:10:41.480
Okay! Hassam!

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:43.200
Use a Steel-type move!

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:44.700
Metal Claw!

00:10:52.450 --> 00:10:53.170
Hassam!

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.850
Return, Hassam!

00:11:08.790 --> 00:11:10.330
The Kyukon...!

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:13.980
Go! This is crazy!

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:15.970
We’re gonna get blown away...

00:11:17.050 --> 00:11:19.890
I have to come up with something!

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:22.120
Go!

00:11:22.120 --> 00:11:23.740
Satoshi!

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:33.470
Pocket Monsters!

00:11:49.690 --> 00:11:51.440
Sarunori...

00:11:57.460 --> 00:11:58.610
Pikachu...

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:03.480
Oh, that’s right... We...

00:12:03.480 --> 00:12:05.940
We were caught in the blizzard...

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:09.930
A Manyula!

00:12:09.930 --> 00:12:12.910
Did they rescue us?

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:15.500
Excuse me...

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:17.730
Seeing weaklings annoys me.

00:12:19.450 --> 00:12:21.190
As soon as the blizzard ends, leave.

00:12:22.620 --> 00:12:24.390
I have something important to d—

00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:25.840
You’re disqualified.

00:12:27.130 --> 00:12:29.570
Were it not for me,
you’d be dead.

00:12:29.570 --> 00:12:32.280
Both you <i>and</i> your Pokémon.

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:34.620
Hold on!

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:36.300
What do you mean, “disqualified”?

00:12:36.300 --> 00:12:39.830
He’s probably part of Project Mew.

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:43.350
Isn’t that right, Mr. Tsurugi?

00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:47.410
You can go ahead and
forget that name.

00:12:53.180 --> 00:12:54.930
Hey, Mr. Tsurugi...

00:12:54.930 --> 00:12:56.910
Is he really disqualified?

00:12:58.310 --> 00:13:01.410
Um...
Can I ask you one question?

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:05.490
Why is an Alolan Kyukon here?

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:08.140
Pokémon Hunters.

00:13:09.880 --> 00:13:11.970
They poached it for money,

00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:15.420
but their airplane crashed
while carrying it.

00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:16.810
It fled up here.

00:13:16.810 --> 00:13:20.750
I get it. That’s why it acted like that
when it saw us...

00:13:22.670 --> 00:13:24.190
Then, if you catch it...?

00:13:25.540 --> 00:13:27.700
I’ll return it to Lanakila Mountain.

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:29.680
So that’s it...

00:13:37.470 --> 00:13:39.210
As you promised, leave.

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:41.750
No!

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:43.130
What?

00:13:43.130 --> 00:13:46.150
There’s still time
before the deadline.

00:13:46.150 --> 00:13:49.500
And Tsurugi,
you’re going to look for Kyukon, right?

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:51.650
What of it?

00:13:51.650 --> 00:13:54.760
I want to get Kyukon
back to its home, too!

00:13:54.760 --> 00:13:55.840
Me, too!

00:13:58.150 --> 00:14:00.900
How will you find it with no clues?

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:03.200
I thought of something earlier.

00:14:03.200 --> 00:14:05.650
If it used to live on Lanakila Mountain,

00:14:06.020 --> 00:14:09.770
then it might want to live somewhere
that looks like Lanakila Mountain, yeah?

00:14:10.720 --> 00:14:11.660
“Looks like”?

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:13.650
Look, over there!

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:19.170
That looks just like
Lanakila Mountain!

00:14:20.810 --> 00:14:22.140
Okay, come on.

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:30.020
No luck...

00:14:32.090 --> 00:14:33.170
Look closer.

00:14:43.050 --> 00:14:45.110
It was camouflaging itself.

00:14:45.110 --> 00:14:46.660
Kyukon!

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:49.290
We want to take you
back to your home!

00:14:49.290 --> 00:14:51.520
So let us catch you!

00:14:52.750 --> 00:14:54.870
Monster Ball, go!

00:14:59.450 --> 00:15:01.710
Let’s go, Aceburn!

00:15:01.710 --> 00:15:02.840
Lightning Speed!

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:07.300
That’s Magical Shine!

00:15:10.430 --> 00:15:11.640
Aceburn!

00:15:13.090 --> 00:15:14.140
Are you okay?

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:21.520
Blaze Kick!

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:29.070
Now it’s using Aurora Veil?

00:15:31.430 --> 00:15:32.460
Don’t give up!

00:15:32.460 --> 00:15:35.030
Smash through it with Pyro Ball!

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:42.250
Monster Ball, go!

00:15:47.990 --> 00:15:49.120
What?!

00:15:49.120 --> 00:15:51.260
I didn’t expect to see you here.

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:56.390
What’s that?!

00:15:56.880 --> 00:16:00.520
Regice! Iceberg Pokémon!
Ice type!

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:03.650
It cloaks itself with frigid air
of negative 200 degrees Celsius!.

00:16:03.650 --> 00:16:07.590
It is said to have slept in a glacier
for thousands of years!

00:16:07.590 --> 00:16:09.690
Thousands of years?!

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:13.370
I think I heard something about
its  body being formed during an ice age.

00:16:13.370 --> 00:16:17.760
Regice is an important Pokémon
for studying the origin of Pokémon as a whole.

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:23.920
Pikachu! 100,000 Volts!

00:16:29.050 --> 00:16:31.230
Go! Leave this to me!

00:16:31.230 --> 00:16:32.880
Thanks, Satoshi!

00:16:35.370 --> 00:16:36.450
Kyukon!

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:40.440
I want to help you!

00:16:40.440 --> 00:16:42.640
Please, let me catch you!

00:16:46.150 --> 00:16:47.310
Kyukon!

00:16:54.970 --> 00:16:56.320
Hold on!

00:16:57.310 --> 00:16:58.950
Trust me!

00:17:01.800 --> 00:17:04.400
Come back to Alola!

00:17:05.850 --> 00:17:09.540
Back to your home,
Lanakila Mountain!

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:28.520
Are you sure?

00:17:33.910 --> 00:17:34.840
Here goes.

00:17:44.170 --> 00:17:48.960
Kyukon: Alolan Form’s data
will be added to the index!

00:17:55.170 --> 00:17:57.120
Satoshi! Pikachu!

00:17:59.230 --> 00:18:00.680
Stand back.

00:18:04.310 --> 00:18:05.480
Destroyer Beam?!

00:18:06.380 --> 00:18:07.370
Let’s go.

00:18:14.510 --> 00:18:15.450
What...?!

00:18:15.450 --> 00:18:17.490
I’ve never seen that Pokémon before!

00:18:18.380 --> 00:18:24.390
Wulaosu. Single Strike Style.
Martial Arts Pokémon. Fighting/Evil type.

00:18:24.390 --> 00:18:26.000
The evolved form of Dakuma.

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:28.120
A strong believer in the one-hit KO.

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:32.380
Its strategy is to leap in close to foes
and land a devastating blow with a hardened fist.

00:18:33.250 --> 00:18:34.470
Dark Blow.

00:18:41.830 --> 00:18:44.020
Wulaosu. That’s enough.

00:18:46.110 --> 00:18:47.520
I’ll come back for you.

00:18:48.170 --> 00:18:50.270
Behave yourself until then.

00:18:57.290 --> 00:18:59.320
It’s time. We’re heading back.

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:00.640
Right!

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:06.700
I’m warming back up...

00:19:14.030 --> 00:19:16.210
I’ve verified the Alolan Kyukon.

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:18.350
You can leave the rest to us.

00:19:18.350 --> 00:19:20.390
Right. Please take care of it!

00:19:20.390 --> 00:19:22.110
Go, Satoshi.

00:19:23.390 --> 00:19:25.430
Thank you for rescuing Kyukon.

00:19:26.650 --> 00:19:27.740
It’s nothing...

00:19:27.740 --> 00:19:30.730
I was just focused on getting it
back to Lanakila Mountain.

00:19:30.730 --> 00:19:33.560
Also, I should tell you this.

00:19:33.560 --> 00:19:37.820
What you cleared
was not an official mission.

00:19:38.930 --> 00:19:43.280
It was a test to determine
if you were fit to enter Project Mew.

00:19:43.280 --> 00:19:44.320
What do you mean?

00:19:44.320 --> 00:19:50.200
In other words, only now
has Go been accepted as an official challenger.

00:19:50.200 --> 00:19:54.580
Oh! So that’s what Shigeru meant
when he said it wasn’t gonna be easy!

00:19:55.340 --> 00:19:57.350
But Tsurugi told me...

00:19:57.350 --> 00:19:58.450
Quiet.

00:19:59.090 --> 00:20:02.940
Are you doing it? Are you not doing it?
Answer me that, and only that.

00:20:02.940 --> 00:20:05.570
I will! Please accept me!

00:20:07.950 --> 00:20:09.850
That’s great news, Go!

00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:11.690
Even I’m getting fired up now!

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:12.690
Yeah!

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:15.400
But I’ve only just made it
to the starting line!

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:16.280
Good enough!

00:20:16.280 --> 00:20:17.810
Don’t let Shigeru beat you!

00:20:17.810 --> 00:20:18.840
Right!

00:20:22.170 --> 00:20:24.170
Congrats, Go.

00:20:24.890 --> 00:20:26.800
Th-Thank you!

00:20:26.800 --> 00:20:29.730
Tsurugi, I hear Regice appeared.

00:20:29.730 --> 00:20:31.690
I’m analyzing the data now.

00:20:31.690 --> 00:20:33.950
Diligent as always, I see.

00:20:33.950 --> 00:20:37.200
It’s no coincidence that you were the Chaser
with the best score!

00:20:38.040 --> 00:20:40.350
Um, Professor Hodaka!

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:47.290
Mr. Tsurugi said that Regice is an important Pokémon
for studying the origin of all Pokémon.

00:20:47.290 --> 00:20:50.060
Yes. That is what I believe.

00:20:50.060 --> 00:20:53.450
Is that connected with Mew?

00:20:53.450 --> 00:20:55.920
Have you ever given it any thought?

00:20:56.770 --> 00:20:59.190
What are Pokémon?

00:20:59.190 --> 00:21:00.950
Where did they come from?

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:05.660
That’s what I want to solve:
the world’s biggest mystery.

00:21:05.660 --> 00:21:10.180
And I believe the key is Mew,
who holds the genes of all Pokémon,

00:21:10.180 --> 00:21:13.330
and is thought to be
ancestor to all Pokémon.

00:21:13.980 --> 00:21:16.250
That’s why I’m meticulously
studying Mew!

00:21:16.950 --> 00:21:20.400
And that’s the ultimate goal
of Project Mew!

00:21:20.400 --> 00:21:21.470
Wow!

00:21:22.050 --> 00:21:24.480
I really wanna be a member!

00:21:24.480 --> 00:21:26.860
Yeah! And I’ll help you!

00:21:28.700 --> 00:21:29.710
Okay...

00:21:29.710 --> 00:21:34.260
While we head back to the base of Mount Tengan,
shall we look over Regice’s data together?

00:21:34.260 --> 00:21:35.230
Yeah!

00:21:36.010 --> 00:21:39.250
Go was finally able to become
a Project Mew challenger.

00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:43.110
His next task will be his first
Trial Mission!

00:23:07.140 --> 00:23:09.580
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.580 --> 00:23:10.880
Go!

00:23:12.830 --> 00:23:13.690
Oh, no!

00:23:13.690 --> 00:23:15.240
We all got split up!

00:23:16.990 --> 00:23:18.210
Okay, Pikachu!

00:23:18.210 --> 00:23:19.830
Let’s look for everyone!

00:23:19.830 --> 00:23:21.210
Huh? Morpeko?

00:23:22.090 --> 00:23:23.670
Nyarth?

00:23:23.670 --> 00:23:25.500
Eevee?!

00:23:25.500 --> 00:23:26.510
Huh?

00:23:26.510 --> 00:23:27.840
Where’s Sarunori?

00:23:28.430 --> 00:23:30.340
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:30.340 --> 00:23:33.890
The Underground Maze Shuffle Panic?!
